  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116340",
      "title": "Managing HTTP-loaded Data via a Service",
      "lectureOrder": 232,
      "videoOrder": 221,
      "sourceHash": "05347f767615e175f82fd82ac705f48606d33ce6a25b3fc96ada76ac2259742a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 2.82,
          "en": "So now we're fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.82,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "for the available and the favorite places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "and we can add places to the favorite places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 12.06,
          "en": "But if I click on a place like Machu Picchu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.06,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "it doesn't appear down here unless I reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 17.31,
          "en": "And that's, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.31,
          "end": 19.833,
          "en": "typically not the user experience we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.76,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "So what I'd like to do instead is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 25.02,
          "en": "I'd like to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.02,
          "end": 29.22,
          "en": "that we somehow notify the UserPlacesComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.22,
          "end": 31.77,
          "en": "about the place we added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.77,
          "end": 33.69,
          "en": "And there are, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.69,
          "end": 37.113,
          "en": "different approaches we could use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.31,
          "end": 41.37,
          "en": "One approach which I'll use is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 44.61,
          "en": "that I actually wanna manage my userPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 46.893,
          "en": "in this place's service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 51.84,
          "en": "And I actually already have a signal for that in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "And also, a loadedUserPlaces signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 58.503,
          "en": "which is the same signal but exposed as a read-only signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "Because now, we can actually use this signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "and update our loaded places when we loaded places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 73.19,
          "en": "but also use it when we add a new place to our userPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.12,
          "end": 76.59,
          "en": "And I'll start by setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 80.61,
          "en": "and updating this userPlaces signal in this service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.61,
          "end": 83.76,
          "en": "whenever we loaded user places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "For this year in this loadUserPlaces method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 91.65,
          "en": "we can call pipe again on the result of calling fetchPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.65,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "because fetchPlaces yields an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.38,
          "end": 96.6,
          "en": "And even though it is an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.6,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "where we already called pipe before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "we can simply call pipe again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "there's nothing wrong with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 108.15299999999999,
          "en": "So we can call pipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.05,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "and pass the tap operator to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 117.18299999999999,
          "en": "And for that, you must import tap from RXJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.32,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "And the tap operator is an operator you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 125.7,
          "en": "to execute some code as you would do it in subscribe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.7,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "but without subscribing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "So you can pass such an observer object to tap,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "and define what should happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "if that observable emits a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 140.37,
          "en": "emits an error or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 143.55,
          "en": "So here I'm interested in the next value being emitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.55,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "not in errors, but in the next value being emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 150.813,
          "en": "And I know that this will be my user places in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 153.75,
          "en": "And TypeScript knows that too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.75,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "it will be an array of places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 159.243,
          "en": "because that's the kind of data this observable will emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "So I tap into that, and then here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 167.52,
          "en": "I want to set my userPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.52,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "So now I'm targeting this userPlaces signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 176.46,
          "en": "I wanna set that signal here to a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.46,
          "end": 178.65,
          "en": "and that should be the userPlaces I got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 179.973,
          "en": "from this observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.47,
          "end": 184.32,
          "en": "So now, I'm simply using this tap operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.32,
          "end": 187.74,
          "en": "to update some data in this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.74,
          "end": 189.543,
          "en": "without subscribing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.83,
          "end": 193.593,
          "en": "That's what you could use the tap operator for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.76,
          "end": 196.983,
          "en": "Now, why am I doing this here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.27,
          "end": 202.07999999999998,
          "en": "Well, because by managing my userPlaces here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.07999999999998,
          "end": 205.413,
          "en": "I can actually go to the userPlaces component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.31,
          "end": 208.68,
          "en": "and get rid of the next function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "in this observer object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 215.013,
          "en": "and instead only handle the error and complete cases here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 222.17000000000002,
          "en": "and replace this places property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.18,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "which currently manages a signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 226.44,
          "en": "that belongs to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.44,
          "end": 230.8,
          "en": "Replace that with a places property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.81,
          "end": 235.29,
          "en": "that in the end, uses the signal provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.29,
          "end": 237.063,
          "en": "by the places service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.29,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "This loadedUserPlaces signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.44,
          "end": 243.423,
          "en": "which is that read-only signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.31,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "With that, the data that's showing up in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 250.953,
          "en": "is managed in this service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.94,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "whereas errors and the loading state are still handled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 257.55,
          "en": "by this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 257.55,
          "end": 259.53,
          "en": "And that is something you could do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.53,
          "end": 262.47,
          "en": "Again, it's just one way of handling this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.47,
          "end": 263.943,
          "en": "but it's a way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 265.38,
          "end": 267.18,
          "en": "And if you saved it and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.18,
          "end": 269.853,
          "en": "you should therefore still see your places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.724,
          "end": 273.3,
          "en": "You still will not see them instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.3,
          "end": 274.86,
          "en": "when you add new places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.86,
          "end": 278.073,
          "en": "but that's now a second step we'll take care of soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "For the moment, it's just good enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 284.55,
          "en": "that we are able to load the places now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.55,
          "end": 285.75,
          "en": "with help of the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.75,
          "end": 289.05,
          "en": "and with help of this signal in this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.05,
          "end": 291.903,
          "en": "or these two related signals.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
